    "body": "## Problem\r\n- `gv` reselects only primary's region, it doesn't have per-cursor behavior. '< '> are buffer-global and the sandbox restores the primary's marks. The Visual atom containing `gv` was voided anyway, so it never cascaded.\r\n- Same for change-marks (`'[ '] '.`): they are stale after edits from other cursors, not managed per-cursor.\r\n- `McSandbox` saves \"editor state\", which should be owned by the `Context` module.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\nLift more state from `McSandbox` into `Context`. `kCtxCursor` (position, curswant) and `kCtxMarks` (Visual area, change-marks), are owned by `Context` now, as an \"in-memory\" special-case (TODO: support it for the \"serialized\" case?).\r\n\r\n- Classify a `gv` selection as replayable. Manage its state per-cursor. Dot-repeat \".\" after `gv` behaves like Vim (the \"1v\" fallback).\r\n- Save/restore change-marks per-cursor. The primary's change-marks are shifted by edits from other cursors during the cascade.\r\n\r\n`McSandbox` still contains (for now) the view and replay isolation (typeahead/mode, redobuff, search patterns, the active selection).\r\n\r\nBonus:\r\n- `visualmode()` is per-cursor.\r\n- A cursor's `curswant` follows its column when other cursors' edits shift it, instead of the column captured after its own replay.\r\n\r\nfix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/41606\r\n\r\n\r\n",
